maria: Quick sync — onboarding sample app surfaced multiple SDK interop oddities for embeddings + rerank. Wanted to capture here before I open individual bugs.

maria: Symptoms: (1) Node batching helper sometimes returns extra nesting for single-item batches (e.g. [[...vec...]]) vs Python which returns a flat vector. (2) Rerank responses have inconsistent score keys across model rollouts (we've seen `score`, `ranking_score`, `score_v2`). (3) Node auth retry can resend without preserving client idempotency header, causing duplicate side effects.

todd: can you paste a minimal repro?

maria: yep, small snippets below — pared down.

```
// Node (sampleapp helper)
const batch = batching.make([{ text: 'lookup' }]);
// batch => [ [0.01, 0.02, ...] ]  // nested for single input

// Python
b = batching.make(['lookup'])
# b => [0.01, 0.02, ...]  // flat

// Rerank payloads seen:
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "score": 0.81 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "ranking_score": 0.81 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "score_v2": 0.81 }] }

// Auth trace snippet:
[auth] 401 -> refresh -> resend without x-rw-idempotency-token -> server processed twice
```

yun: repro'd the Node nesting locally. Helper code path does an unconditional wrap then consumers sometimes wrap again. We should pick a contract: either helper always returns array-of-vectors (list-of-list) or helper mirrors raw API shape. My vote: helper should always return list-of-list (explicit batch). I'll open a small PR to make that explicit and add unit tests for n=1 and n>1.

anya: For rerank fields, SDK should normalize on read. Fallback priority: score > ranking_score > score_v2 > confidence. Also add a JSON schema assertion in CI so model rollouts that change the field break tests. I can author the SDK patch to accept multiple keys and export a normalized `score` on the public response.

todd: Auth retry is the sticky bit. The Node auth middleware refreshes token and replays request but drops x-rw-idempotency-token. Two options: preserve client idempotency token across retries (preferred) or make retry logic mutate only auth headers and not resend body for non-idempotent endpoints. I'm filing infra ticket.

infra-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-4007: "SDK interop: Node batching shape + rerank key variance + auth retry idempotency". Suggested PRs: prs/8120 (node-batch-contract), prs/8121 (sdk-rerank-normalize), prs/8122 (auth-retry-preserve-idem). Request: include e2e in sampleapp that asserts Node & Python normalized outputs match on a fixed fixture.

maria: Short-term workaround I pushed to the sampleapp template to reduce new-user friction: always normalize embedding shape and map rerank keys before downstream calls. Snippet I used below.

```js
// normalize embeddings to [N][D]
let vecs = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(vecs[0])) vecs = [vecs];

// normalize rerank score
const normalized = res.results.map(r => ({
  id: r.id,
  score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.score_v2 ?? r.confidence
}));
```

yun: Good short-term. I'll land the node helper PR with tests and an explicit docstring: "returns array-of-vectors: [[v1],[v2],...]". That should prevent ambiguous double-wrapping.

anya: I'll add the SDK mapping change + a small CI schema test to catch field renames. Also adding a regression test verifying normalized output shape and score present.

todd: I'll open the infra PR to preserve x-rw-idempotency-token across retries and add an integration test that ensures side-effects are deduped when a token is present.

sdk-ci: CI note — please add an e2e that runs both Node & Py sampleapp flows against a deterministic fixture and asserts: (1) embeddings shape normalized to [N][D], (2) rerank responses normalized to include `score` for each result, (3) no duplicate side-effects in auth retry scenario.

maria: Thanks all. Once PRs land I'll remove the temporary sampleapp shim and update onboarding docs to call out the expected helper contract and the rerank key normalization. Will link logs to DEVEX-4007. :sparkles:
